  <abstract>
    <p>
      This is a mostly personal, Zettelkasten-styled learning and note-taking journal meant to support my self-guided study of various STEM topics including geometric algebra, quantum computing, physics, and neuroscience. It will also serve to document my evolving understanding of these subjects as I work through repositories on Scriber Labs. The goal is not completeness, but clarity: a scaffold for self-guided learning and a resource for anyone who might find these notes useful. Its success is measured by whether it helps cultivate sustained curiosity and a deeper understanding.
    </p>
  </abstract>
